Test fixtures LEAK on bare metal: the native/arm32 byte-ref unit tests build many assemblers + reference-instruction buffers that are allocated and never freed, accumulating a live set larger than the 4 MiB arena. NOT an allocator defect — the SFL reclaiming allocator greened 5 of the 7 formerly-crashing baremetal packages; the free lists are near-empty at exhaustion, so the memory is live, not reclaimable. The old never-reclaiming bump allocator masked this. The leak (a test-fixture leak, or a refcount / compiler defect) is tracked for investigation in explorations/claude-todo.md.
